1.	Introduction
Healthcare accessibility remains a significant challenge in many regions due to geographical barriers limited specialist availability and time constraints with the rapid growth of web technologies healthcare services can now be delivered efficiently through secure online platforms.
The proposed project focuses on the development of a web based remote telemedicine platform that integrates online medical consultation intelligent is search and login waste of hospitals recommendations within a unified system that platform aligns will digital healthcare transformation initiatives encouraged by the Ministry of Health and family welfare to improve healthcare accessibility through online driven solutions
2.	Problem statement
Patients often experienced difficulties in:
1)	identifying the correct specialist for a particular disease
2)	finding nearby hospitals quickly 
3)	booking timely medical consultations 
4)	managing medical records securely 
5)	accessing healthcare information remotely
Traditional healthcare systems are largely dependent dependent on physical visits and manual processes are centralised web based system can significantly improve efficiency accessibility and patient convenience.
3.	Aim of the project
To design and develop a secure scalable and user friendly web based  telemedicine platform that enables disease search hospital discovery and online consultation through our single digital interface.
4.	Objectives
1)	to develop a fully functional web application for tally medicine services
2)	to implement a disease search feature that provides relevant healthcare recommendations.
3)	To integrate a location base hospital Finder using web APIs
4)	to enable secure video consultation between doctor and patients.
5)	To implement electronics medical record (EMR) management.
6)	To ensure data privacy through authentication and encryption mechanism.


5.	Proposed web system overview
The system will be developed using a client server architecture where users access services through a web browser
Intelligent disease search and hospital locator when a user searches for a disease or symptom:
1)	The system displays basic information about the condition.
2)	It identifies relevant medical specialists.
3)	It fetches nearby hospitals using location based services 
(Map API).
4)	it shows available doctors for online consultation.
5)	results can be filtered by specialisation distance and availability.
6)	this feature announces informed decision making and immediate healthcare access.
6.	System modules
1.	Patient module (web interface)
a)	register and login
b)	disease search functionality
c)	appointment booking
d)	access to prescriptions and reports
e)	medical history management
2.	Doctor module (web dashboard)
a)	appointment management
b)	online consultation video integration
c)	prescription generation
d)	patient and record access
3.	Admin module
a)	user and doctor verification
b)	hospital data management
c)	system monitoring
d)	analytics dashboard
4.	Hospital locator module 
a)	location detection via browser
b)	integration with Google Maps API
c)	distance based hospital listing
d)	hospitals specialisation and rating display


